    "rich_text_XmAqYx": {
      "type": "rich-text",
      "settings": {
        "subheading": "",
        "title": "",
        "title_size": 36,
        "title_width": 40,
        "heading_h1": false,
        "text": "<p>The resurgence of business and tourism travel in the post-pandemic world has fueled a boom in hotel renovations and new constructions [2]. Global demand for hospitality upholstery fabrics is expected to grow by 30% between 2023 and 2028. Currently, approximately 67% of the fabrics used in this sector are synthetic, relying heavily on fossil-based raw materials [1].</p><p>On average, each hotel room requires between 11 and 17 m² of upholstery fabric, priced between €7 and €15 per square meter. Based on projected growth, 2 to 6 million new hotel rooms in Europe alone may need upholstering by 2028. With an average fabric weight of 450 g/m², this translates to 11 to 24 thousand tons of material—nearly all of it synthetic.</p><p>Now, imagine if all of this synthetic fabric were replaced with <strong>PEEL</strong>—a renewable, plant-based alternative developed by Monteiro Fabrics. This single shift could eliminate the need for 19 to 41 thousand tons of fossil-based inputs globally, replacing them with renewable resources that are significantly more biodegradable and less ecotoxic (according to Monteiro Fabrics internal composting studies and life cycle assessments)<br/><br/></p>",
        "image": "shopify://shop_images/1100vegan-white_f21b00d3-9446-4bea-94fb-b670e1aef7f9.png",
        "image_width": 60,
        "button_label": "",
        "button_link": "",
        "button_style": "auto",
        "text_alignment": "center",
        "enlarge_text": true,
        "full_width": false,
        "no_padding_bottom": false,
        "color_scheme": "standard",
        "color_bg": "",
        "color_text": ""
      }
    },
    "1d862462-6fb2-4740-a51d-020f8acd47dd": {
      "type": "image-with-text",
      "settings": {
        "subheading": "Fossil Based Material Savings with PEEL",
        "title": "65% Biobased *",
        "title_size": 28,
        "title_width": 12,
        "text": "<p>Using PEEL as an alternative to synthetic upholstery textiles in the hospitality sector – estimated projection for 2028.</p><p> -</p><p><strong>Region | Estimated Savings</strong></p><p><strong>Europe | 5,000 – 10,000 ton</strong></p><p><strong>North America | 5,000 – 11,000 ton</strong></p><p><strong>Asia Pacific | 7,000 – 14,000 ton</strong></p><p><strong>Other Regions | 3,000 – 6,000 ton</strong></p><p>  </p><p><strong>➤ Total 19,000 – 41,000 ton</strong></p><p><strong> -</strong></p><p><em>*ASTM D6866-22-Method B</em></p><p></p>",
        "button_label": "PEEL COLECTION",
        "button_link": "shopify://pages/peel-collection",
        "text_alignment": "center",
        "text_width": 50,
        "button_style": "auto",
        "image": "shopify://shop_images/PEEL-COLLECTION_17d0204d-b0fc-4a44-8c1c-09ff8dd148d6.jpg",
